    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95934" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπίλος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span> (B), ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>spot, fleck,
			blemish</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dorio
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				7.297c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. αἵματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					13.11.3
				</span></i>
			 (pl.); on the moon, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.921f
			</span></i>; on the face or body, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Am.</u>
				15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Artem.
				5.67
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Decl.</u>
				26.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				12.26.2
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>stain</i> of impurity or vice, <i><span class="en">
				Lysis
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>VP</u>
				17.76
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Eph.</u>
				5.27
			</span></i>; of persons, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				4.24
			</span></i> (cj.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>2 Ep.Pet.</u>
				2.13
			</span></i>. (
				Att.
			 use <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κηλίς</span> acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				21
			</span></i>.) [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπῖλος</span> Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				2.920
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ</span> in the
			equiv. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπιλάς</span> (B) and in the compd.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσπιλος</span>.]</div>
